:: Revelation Temple Review
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<npc Jordan>>
<<person1>>
<<if !_dutyOffice or $temple_rank isnot 'monk'>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<span class='gold bold'><<lanSwitch 'Ordination review' '司祭任职审查'>></span><br><br>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Jordan lays out the records for the missing member of the flock and the pilgrimage for the spear. "Before we speak of appointing you as a priest, we must check the tasks already entrusted to you."
    <<He>> opens your handovers and field reports. "When the dark knocks, the flock needs someone to protect them. Before I entrust you with that duty, tell me how you kept everyone safe during the watch in the lower passage."
  <<option 'CN'>>
    约旦把寻找失踪教徒与取回长矛的两份记录摆在桌上。“谈司祭的任命之前，我们先核对交托给你的事情。”
    <<He>>翻开交接记录与外勤报告。“黑暗叩门时，教徒需要有人保护。把这份职责交给你之前，我想听听，你在下层通道守望时，是怎样照看同行的人。”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<temple-duty-requirements>>
<<if _dutyReady and Time.hour lt 17>>
  <<socialiseicon 'ask'>>
  <<temple-duty-action `['Report your work and the watch to Jordan (0:20)', '向约旦汇报职责与守望的经过 (0:20)']` 20 'Revelation Temple Review Choice'>>
    <<temple-duty-check>>
    <<if _dutyReady>>
      <<set $TempleDuties.review to true>>
    <</if>>
  <</temple-duty-action>>
  <br>
<<else>>
  <span class='lblue'><<lanSwitch 'Complete the outstanding duties before the interview. Leave an hour for the interview and oath before the duties desk closes.' '先完成尚未履行的职责。请在职务桌关闭前，留出一小时参加面谈与宣誓。'>></span><br>
<</if>>
<br>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Revelation Temple Review Choice
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<npc Jordan>>
<<person1>>
<<if !_dutyReady or !$TempleDuties.review>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Jordan reads the account of the rescued member before the record of the returned spear. "One brought a person home. One brought back what we had entrusted to you. Neither was safe work. I'm thankful you returned too." <<He>> asks which parts you could not have managed alone.
    A clerk comes to the door and reports that a novice is afraid to return to the lower storeroom. Jordan turns to you. "What would you say if they came to you for help?"
  <<option 'CN'>>
    约旦先读获救教徒的记录，再看交还长矛的那一页。“一件把人带回家，一件带回了我们交托给你的东西。都不是安全的工作。我也很庆幸你回来了。”<<He>>问起哪些事情是你独自做不到的。
    一名侍从来到门口，说有位见习教徒害怕再去下层储藏室。约旦转向你，问道：“要是对方向你求助，你会怎么回答？”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon>>
<<temple-duty-action `['Say you would listen, then offer to check the room together (0:05)', '回答：先听见习教徒说完，再陪对方检查房间 (0:05)']` 5 'Revelation Temple Review Answer'>>
  <<set $TempleDuties.oath to 'care'>>
<</temple-duty-action>>
<br>
<<socialiseicon>>
<<temple-duty-action `['Say the novice should obey and return alone (0:05)', '回答：见习教徒应当服从，独自回去 (0:05)']` 5 'Revelation Temple Review Answer'>>
  <<set $TempleDuties.oath to 'obedience'>>
<</temple-duty-action>>
<br>
<br>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Revelation Temple Review Answer
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<npc Jordan>>
<<person1>>
<<if !_dutyReady or !$TempleDuties.review>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<if $TempleDuties.oath is 'obedience'>>
  <<language>>
    <<option 'EN'>>
      Jordan closes the book. "Obedience doesn't tell us whether the room is safe. You know more than that novice does; you must use it to help them." <<He>> leaves the interview unfinished. You may return after considering <<his>> answer.
    <<option 'CN'>>
      约旦合上书。“服从不能证明房间安全。你比那个见习教徒知道得更多，就应当用这些知识帮对方。”<<He>>没有继续面谈。想清楚这番话后，你可以再来。
  <</language>>
<<else>>
  <<language>>
    <<option 'EN'>>
      "Good," Jordan says. "You need not promise there is no danger. But promise that you will check for yourself, and that you will not leave someone there alone just to prove they should not be afraid."
      <<if $auriga_scar gt 0>>
        There is one more thing you could tell <<him>> about: what the Elk left with you. You can also keep that experience private.
      <</if>>
    <<option 'CN'>>
      “很好，”约旦说，“你不必保证那里没有危险。但你应当答应，会亲自核实，也不会为了证明对方不该害怕，就把人独自留在那里。”
      <<if $auriga_scar gt 0>>
        还有一件事，你可以向<<him>>说明：麋鹿留在你身上的影响。你也可以不谈这段经历。
      <</if>>
  <</language>>
  <br><br>
  <<if $auriga_scar gt 0>>
    <<socialiseicon 'ask'>>
    <<temple-duty-action `['Explain the Elk’s mark before the oath (0:10)', '宣誓前说明麋鹿留下的影响 (0:10)']` 10 'Revelation Temple Oath'>>
      <<set $TempleDuties.declaration to 'scar'>>
    <</temple-duty-action>>
    <br>
  <</if>>
  <<templeicon 'altar'>>
  <<lanLink ['Keep your experiences private and consider whether to take the oath', '先不谈私人经历，考虑是否宣誓'] 'Revelation Temple Oath'>>
    <<set $TempleDuties.declaration to 'private'>>
  <</lanLink>>
  <br>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Revelation Temple Oath
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<npc Jordan>>
<<person1>>
<<if !_dutyReady or !$TempleDuties.review or $TempleDuties.oath isnot 'care'>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.declaration is 'scar'>>
      Jordan listens, then rests a hand beside your report. "Come to us if it troubles you again, child."
    <</if>>
    Jordan places the appointment on the little table beside the fire, next to your record of the returned spear. "Will you serve God, keep your sacred chastity and protect the flock?" A priest by the door folds a stained cloth. Jordan continues, "Remember the vows you make here when you leave the temple too, child."
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.declaration is 'scar'>>
      约旦听完，把手放在报告旁。“它再次困扰你时，来找我们，孩子。”
    <</if>>
    约旦把任命书放在炉边的小桌上，旁边是你取回长矛的记录。“你愿意侍奉主、守持神圣贞洁，保护神殿的教徒吗？”门边的司祭叠起一块沾着血的布。约旦接着说：“离开神殿以后，也要记住你在这里许下的誓言，孩子。”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<templeicon 'altar'>>
<<temple-duty-action `['Make the vows to Jordan and accept appointment as a priest (0:20)', '向约旦宣誓，接受司祭任命 (0:20)']` 20 'Revelation Temple Ordained'>>
  <<temple-duty-check>>
  <<if _dutyReady and $TempleDuties.review and $TempleDuties.oath is 'care'>>
    <<temple-ordain-player>>
  <</if>>
<</temple-duty-action>>
<br>
<<templeicon 'altar'>>
<<lanLink ['Invite Robin or Sydney to share the appointment ceremony', '邀请罗宾或悉尼一同参加任命仪式'] 'Revelation Temple Shared Oath'>>
  <<set $TempleDuties.party to []>>
<</lanLink>>
<br>
<<getouticon>>
<<lanLink ['Ask for more time', '再考虑一段时间'] 'Revelation Temple Office'>>
<</lanLink>>
<br>

:: Revelation Temple Ordained
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<npc Jordan>>
<<person1>>
<<if $TempleDuties.ordained lt 0 or $temple_rank isnot 'priest'>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Jordan signs your appointment beside the fire. "You are a priest of our order now," <<he>> says quietly. <<He>> leaves the duties book closed. "There will be work tomorrow. For now, stay here and warm yourself." The priest at the door lays a clean strip of linen beside you.
  <<option 'CN'>>
    约旦在炉边签下你的任命书。“现在，你是我们教团的司祭了。”<<He>>轻声说，没有打开职务簿。“明天还有事要做。现在，先在这里暖暖身子吧。”门边的司祭在你身旁放下一条干净的布巾。
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Temple Duties Review Widgets [widget]
<<widget 'temple-duty-requirements'>>
  <<if !_flockRescued or !_spearReturned or $TempleDuties.trial_day lt 0>>
    <ul class='journal'>
    <<if !_flockRescued>>
      <li><<lanSwitch 'Rescue the missing temple member from the manor on Danube Street.' '从多瑙河街的宅邸救回失踪的神殿成员。'>></li>
    <</if>>
    <<if !_spearReturned>>
      <li><<lanSwitch 'Bring the golden spear back to Jordan.' '将金色长矛交还约旦。'>></li>
    <</if>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.trial_day lt 0>>
      <li><<lanSwitch 'Complete the watch in the lower passage.' '完成下层通道的守望。'>></li>
    <</if>>
    </ul>
  <</if>>
<</widget>>


<<widget 'temple-ordain-player'>>
  <<if $temple_rank is 'monk' and _dutyReady>>
    <<set $temple_rank to 'priest'>>
    <<set $TempleDuties.companion_day to -1>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.ordained lt 0>>
      <<set $TempleDuties.ordained to Math.floor(Time.days)>>
      <<npcincr Jordan love 3>>
      <<famegood 20 null true>>
    <</if>>
  <</if>>
<</widget>>
